  "texto": "# Arriving\n@energy 2\n> Speak slowly, like walking someone to sleep.\n\n[slow][soft]Find a comfortable position, in bed or in an armchair.\nLet your body rest fully on whatever holds it.\nClose your eyes whenever you like.\nNotice your eyelids growing heavy.\n[breathe]\nOutside, it starts to rain.\nListen to the first drops tapping on the glass, one by one.\n[breathe]\nYou don't have to go anywhere now.\nYou're indoors, with a warm blanket over your legs.\nCan you hear the rain becoming steadier? [up][/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The sound\n@energy 2\n> Soft, unhurried.\n\n[soft]The rain falls on the roof, on the trees and on the empty street.\nIt's a constant sound that asks for nothing.\n[breathe]\nLet your breathing follow its rhythm.\nBreathe in as the drops fall.\nBreathe out as the water runs down the window.\nBreathe in again, without hurry, and breathe out with ease.\n[breathe]\nEach drop that slides down the glass carries a thought away.\nYou don't have to stop them: just watch them go.\nOne, and another, and another.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# The room\n@energy 1\n> Very soft. Like a whisper.\n\n[slow][soft]Imagine the room in dim light, warm and quiet.\nMaybe it smells of tea, of wood or of clean sheets.\n[breathe]\nFeel the weight of the soft blanket on your legs.\nYour feet loosen, your ankles let go.\nYour knees rest.\nYour hands open on the blanket, holding nothing.\n[breathe]\nOutside, the storm passes by.\nInside, everything is calm.\nHere, you are **safe**.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Letting go\n@energy 1\n> Slow, almost a whisper.\n\n[slow][soft]Now the rain grows finer, almost a murmur.\nLet your shoulders drop a little more.\nRelax your forehead, your jaw and your tongue.\n[breathe]\nIf a worry comes, imagine writing it on the fogged-up window.\nWatch the drops wash it away, little by little.\nOne by one, your worries turn into water.\n[breathe]\nDo you notice your body growing heavier? [up]\nThere's nothing to fix tonight, and nothing to plan for tomorrow.\nJust listen, and enjoy the simple pleasure of the rain.[/soft][/slow]\n[pause 3s]\n\n# Coming back\n@energy 2\n> Gently, coming back to the present.\n\n[soft]Little by little, the rain stops.\nOnly a few drops are left, falling from the roof.\nThe air smells of wet earth, clean and fresh.\n[breathe]\nBring your attention to your breath, now slow and deep.\nIf you're going to sleep, stay here, in this calm.\nIf you're going on with your day, move your fingers and toes.\n[breathe]\nStretch your arms gently.\nOpen your eyes whenever you like.\nTake a little of this silence with you.[/soft]\n[pause 3s]\n"
