  "ppm": 155,
  "texto": "# Headlines\n@energy 4\n> Sports newscast voice: clear, with controlled energy.\n\nGood evening, and welcome to this special sports edition.\nThis afternoon, the final of the Valley Women's League was played, a league **invented** for this newscast.\nThe Rio Claro Hawks and Puerto Alba Athletic packed the city stadium.\nMore than twelve thousand people watched the match from the stands.\nThe result was decided in the final **minutes**, with a play no one will forget.\nIn this edition: the match summary, the player of the night and the party in the streets.\nWe'll also hear what the coaches said after the final whistle.\nAll the teams, players and places in this story are fictional.\nLet's go to the **first** half.\n[pause]\n\n# The first half\n@energy 4\n> A brisk pace, no shouting.\n\nThe match began with Athletic determined to press from the very first minute.\nIn the twelfth minute, striker Paula Rivas opened the scoring with a **perfect** header.\nThe home crowd answered with drums, flags and huge applause.\nThe Hawks were slow to react and lost several balls in midfield.\nTheir goalkeeper, Valentina Soto, prevented a second goal with two **key** saves.\nCould the visitors change the story? [up]\nJust before halftime, captain Andrea Molina hit the crossbar with a free kick.\nThe whole stadium held its breath for a second.\nThe first half ended **one** to nothing for Puerto Alba Athletic.\n[pause]\n\n# The second half\n@energy 4\n> The tension rises: firm and clear.\n\nIn the second half, the Hawks came out with a different **attitude**.\nTheir coach made two changes and moved Molina forward, closer to the opposing goal.\nIn the sixty-eighth minute came the equalizer, after a long pass and a low shot across the goal.\nFrom then on, the match swung from end to end.\nBoth teams had clear chances, but the goalkeepers stayed alert.\nJust as everyone expected a penalty shootout, the play of the night arrived.\nIn the ninety-second minute, Molina won the ball in midfield.\nShe surged forward, slipped past two defenders and fired a **low** shot into the far corner.\nThe stadium erupted in a roar that lasted several minutes!\nFinal score: Hawks two, Athletic **one**.\n[pause]\n\n# Player of the night\n@energy 4\n> Closing report on the match.\n\nPlayer of the match was, without a doubt, captain Andrea Molina.\nAt thirty-one, she was playing her last **final** before retiring.\n\"I've dreamed of this goal since I was a little girl,\" she said, her shirt still soaked.\nThe Hawks' coach praised the team's work and its patience in difficult moments.\nAt Athletic, the coach congratulated his players and promised to face next season with more strength.\n\"We lost a final, but we didn't lose our **pride**,\" he told reporters.\nMeanwhile, thousands of fans poured into the main square of Rio Claro to celebrate.\nThere was music, car horns and fireworks until the early **hours**.\nTomorrow, the trophy, now the city's greatest treasure, will tour its schools.\n[pause]\n\n# Sign-off\n@energy 4\n> Sports newscast close: calm.\n\nAnd finally, what's next for both teams.\nThe new season of the Valley Women's League will begin in three months.\nThe Hawks have already confirmed **two** young players from their youth academy.\nAthletic, for its part, will be looking for a new defender.\nUnder its new rules, the league will also schedule more matches at family-friendly times.\nIt was an incredible final, clean and full of emotion.\nRemember, everything you heard is fiction, although the passion for sport is very **real**.\nThat was tonight's sports summary.\nThank you for joining us, and see you **next** time. [down]\n"
